---
<Prose title="Affiliate Disclosure: How Enthusiast Review Makes Money" h1="Affiliate Disclosure" description="Enthusiast Review earns commissions from Amazon and other retailers on some links. Commissions never change which PC parts we pick or how we rank them.">
  <p>{SITE.name} is reader-supported. When you click a link to a retailer such as Amazon and buy something, we may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.</p>
  <p>{SITE.name} participates in the Amazon Services LLC Associates Program, an affiliate advertising program designed to provide a means for sites to earn advertising fees by advertising and linking to Amazon.com. As an Amazon Associate we earn from qualifying purchases.</p>
  <h2>What commissions do not change</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Which parts we recommend, or their order on a list.</li>
    <li>The {SITE.score} a part receives.</li>
    <li>What we say about a part's weaknesses.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Manufacturers cannot pay for placement and never review a page before it is published. Affiliate links on this site are marked <code>rel="sponsored"</code>.</p>
  <p>Questions? Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
</Prose>
